In a Next.js 16 App Router project without Cache Components, this page uses no request-time APIs and no uncached data:

```tsx
// app/about/page.tsx
export default function About() {
  return <h1>About us</h1>
}
```

How is it rendered in production?

Analytics needs missing products in the previous question to return a real HTTP 404. The page is:

```tsx
export default async function Page({ params }: PageProps<'/p/[id]'>) {
  const { id } = await params
  return (
    <Suspense fallback={<Skeleton />}>
      <Product id={id} />
    </Suspense>
  )
}
```

Which change achieves that?

With Cache Components, this layout wraps `/shop/[slug]`, and most slugs are not returned by `generateStaticParams`:

```tsx
export default async function Layout({ children, params }: LayoutProps<'/shop/[slug]'>) {
  const { slug } = await params
  return (
    <div>
      <Sidebar />
      <h1>{slug}</h1>
      {children}
    </div>
  )
}
```

What is the problem, and what fix do the docs recommend?
